> data("alfonsino")

> lfd <- FLQuantLen(lfd_long_to_wide(as.data.frame(lfd_alfonsino)), 
+     unit = "cm", midL = FALSE)

> lhpar <- FLPar(linf = 55.7, k = 0.08, M = 0.162, L50 = 31.1859, 
+     a = 0.004721956/1000, b = 3.146168)

> stklen <- stocklen(lfd, lhpar, m_model = "constant")

> sf <- c("dsnormal", "logistic")

> cbg <- c(0.7, 0.3)

> set0 <- list(CVL = 0.1, obs_model = "dm", dm_theta = "saturating")

> fit <- fiticc(lfd, stklen, sel_fun = sf, catch_by_gear = cbg, 
+     settings = set0)
FLicc: the Dirichlet-multinomial precision is estimated best from raw counts or an effective sample size of at least 500 per gear and year (median here: Trawl 600, Gillnet 400).

